# Every entry below says why it is ignored: SECRET (credentials or tokens),
# OPERATIONAL DATA (private or per-machine state that must never reach this
# public repository), or REBUILDABLE (a cache or build output regenerated on
# demand). An entry with no reason is one the next reader un-ignores. Git reads
# no trailing comment on a pattern line, so each reason sits on its own line.

# SECRET: credentials. The template is tracked, empty structure only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the live platform settings. Each OS has a TRACKED template
# (settings.local.linux.json / .macos.json / .windows.json); the live file is
# machine-local (absolute paths, per-machine permission grants) and MERGES the
# template on each setup run.
.claude/settings.local.json
# OPERATIONAL DATA: backups and the atomic-write temp file from
# scripts/merge-platform-settings.py; copies of the live file above. Since
# 2026-10-16 setup-platform.sh sends the backup to the data repository
# (runtime:settings-backup/state); this covers a clone with no data repository.
.claude/settings.local.json.bak-*
.claude/settings.local.json.tmp

# REBUILDABLE: Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# REBUILDABLE: pytest-cov artifacts.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: OS metadata files.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# OPERATIONAL DATA: clipboard images (transient screenshots via cv command).
outputs/clipboard/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Telegram group backup artifacts (JSON dumps, downloaded
# media, throwaway helper scripts).
outputs/telegram-groups-backup/

# SECRET: browser cookies imported via /setup-browser-cookies.
outputs/browser/cookies.json

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Chromium profile caches from Playwright and CDP automation.
outputs/browser/chrome-profile/
outputs/**/.profile/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: LinkedIn scrape artifacts (authenticated DOM dumps, may
# contain PII).
outputs/browser/linkedin-*.html
outputs/browser/linkedin-*.md
outputs/browser/linkedin-*.json
outputs/browser/li-debug.*

# SECRET: service sessions (auth tokens, runtime state).
.sessions/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: editor swap and backup files, editor and agent tool state.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.zed/
.agent/
.agents/
.kiro/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: MobaXterm workspace artifacts (legacy, kept as safeguard).
Desktop
LauncherFolder
MyDocuments
slash/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: per-instance operator identity (name, slug, voice, email).
# The engine ships scripts/operator.example.yaml; the engine-local
# config/operator.yaml is the fallback on a clone with no data repository.
config/operator.yaml

# OPERATIONAL DATA: which inference host serves THIS machine. Every address in
# it is a fact about one computer; the engine ships
# config/inference-hosts.example.yaml, and an absent live file is a valid setup.
config/inference-hosts.yaml

# OPERATIONAL DATA: per-clone identity and heartbeat, and leftover clones of the
# retired corporate and CRM-central repositories (executive model removed
# 2026-09-25), which old clones may still hold.
.workspace-identity.json
.heartbeat.json
.corporate-repo/
.crm-central-repo/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Firecrawl cache under the data overlay (scraped web
# content, potentially sensitive).
outputs/browser/firecrawl-cache/

# REBUILDABLE: DocParse cache. No trailing slash: the cache-store gate asks git
# about that exact spelling (2026-09-14).
.cache/docparse

# VACATED 2026-09-25 (HOS-5 section 7): no engine code writes any entry in this
# block any more; each writer uses the data repository's runtime store, and
# scripts/dev/engine-dir-writes.py refuses a new one. Still ignored because
# existing checkouts hold old contents until HELM moves them.
# OPERATIONAL DATA: sentinel state, logs and PID; sync state.
.sentinel/
.sync/
# OPERATIONAL DATA: scraped web content, potentially sensitive.
.cache/firecrawl/
# REBUILDABLE: the 24h Models API cache.
.cache/claude-models.json
# OPERATIONAL DATA: this machine's day-mode marker and full-run verdict, and the
# revision its nightly last ran on; a committed copy would hand every other
# clone a green run that never happened there.
.cache/day-mode/
.cache/nightly-refresh/
# REBUILDABLE: per-checkout test verdicts, keyed by a digest of the tree.
.cache/test-verdicts.db
.cache/test-verdicts.db-journal
.cache/test-verdicts.db-wal
.cache/test-verdicts.db-shm
# OPERATIONAL DATA: content-gate verdicts; the key derives from a token set
# harvested from the private overlay.
.cache/content-verdicts.db
.cache/content-verdicts.db-journal
.cache/content-verdicts.db-wal
.cache/content-verdicts.db-shm
# OPERATIONAL DATA: checkout scratch.
.tmp/
# OPERATIONAL DATA: daemon PIDs, logs and sentinels (sync-exchange),
# and the retired bridge daemon's token, port and telemetry.
.sync-exchange/
.daemon-state/
# OPERATIONAL DATA: hook state; its content hashes read as high-entropy strings.
.claude/state/
# OPERATIONAL DATA: per-machine logs and state; the recall-op log can hold
# private query text and paths.
.logs/
.state/
# OPERATIONAL DATA: safe-push live status files.
.push-state/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: per-machine data directory of paths.py (data_dir).
.data/

# REBUILDABLE: Puppeteer's browser cache (scripts/marp_render.py). It resolves to
# `$PUPPETEER_CACHE_DIR`, else `~/.cache/puppeteer`; a relative
# PUPPETEER_CACHE_DIR would land a ~400 MB browser under the repo root, where
# `git add -A` would commit it. No trailing slash: `git check-ignore` cannot tell
# that a path which does not exist would be a directory.
.cache/puppeteer

# OPERATIONAL DATA: HEADING OS 2 judgement verdicts, keyed by the operator's real
# overlay paths. The writer retired 2026-09-20; the rule outlives it on purpose,
# because a machine that ran it still holds the store. No trailing slash, for
# the same reason as the entry above.
.cache/heading-os-2-judgement

# OPERATIONAL DATA: auto-generated sync state (calendar, email, linkedin).
outputs/_sync/

# REBUILDABLE: MARP renders, regenerable from source; the sources stay tracked.
outputs/deliverables/presentations/*.pdf
outputs/deliverables/presentations/*.html
outputs/deliverables/presentations/*.png
!outputs/deliverables/presentations/marp-source/
!outputs/deliverables/presentations/marp-source/**

# OPERATIONAL DATA: scheduled tasks runtime state.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the commit message a YARD prepares for HELM to commit, when
# it is written inside the checkout. Untracked and unignored it would read as a
# data artifact sitting in the engine clone (2026-09-21).
.commit-message-*.txt

# OPERATIONAL DATA: browser preference backups (high-entropy browser data).
outputs/operations/system/backups/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: email intelligence transient runtime files (Exchange
# message IDs).
outputs/operations/email-intelligence/_*
outputs/operations/email-intelligence/state.json

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Office lock/owner files.
~$*

# OPERATIONAL DATA: DocParse raw outputs (may contain sensitive scraped data).
outputs/intel/docparse/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: sensitive closed-project archives, never tracked in any git
# history.
outputs/projects/

# SECRET: Atticus book-writing backups (contain JWT session tokens).
**/atticus-backup-*.json

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the removed secure vault; never committed.
_secure/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: setup wizard state (PII, per-machine).
.setup/

# REBUILDABLE: migration mirror clones (full git history, regenerable from origin).
outputs/operations/migrations/*.git/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: CRM aggregation outputs (the aggregator was removed with the
# executive model on 2026-09-25, so any copy is stale).
crm/aggregated/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: skill scratch (drafts, helper scripts, intermediate artifacts).
outputs/_tmp/
outputs/_temp/
outputs/_yt_tmp/
scripts/_scratch/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Superpowers plugin runtime state.
.superpowers/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: design records, plans, specs and ADRs. The engine is public,
# but how it was built is not; they live in the data repository (registry name
# `spec-docs`), never in the engine clone.
docs/superpowers/
docs/design/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: git worktrees created inside the checkout.
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the operator's own threads, never committed.
threads/personal/
threads/archive/**/personal/


# OPERATIONAL DATA: outreach send log, pipeline touch log and inbox dismiss log
# (private notes about recipients and deals, Exchange conversation IDs).
outputs/operations/fundraising/**/_send-log.jsonl
outputs/operations/pipeline/_touch-log.jsonl
outputs/operations/email-intelligence/_dismiss-log.jsonl

# OPERATIONAL DATA: CRM migration staging and backup (one-shot).
crm/.migration-staging/
crm/.migration-backup/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: eval-drift daemon runtime (PID, rotated log, stop sentinel).
.eval-drift/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: a launcher the retired Windows bridge installer generated;
# old clones may still hold one, with machine paths in it.
scripts/launch-bridge-daemon.bat

# REBUILDABLE: service-host state mirror, regenerated frequently.
datastore/operations/service-mirror/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: daemon runtime state files (per-machine, continuously
# rewritten). The surrounding directories still hold tracked content.
datastore/operations/eval-drift/errors.log
datastore/operations/eval-drift/state.json
# REBUILDABLE: fundraising build intermediates.
outputs/operations/fundraising/**/_build/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Marp skill scratch sources (dot-prefixed per-run temps).
.*.marp-src-*.md

# REBUILDABLE: local associative-memory index, engine-side code index, and the
# CodeGraph index (`codegraph init` recreates it).
.memory-index/
.memory-index-code/
.codegraph/

# REBUILDABLE: Odin collect recency marker (absence widens the --since window).
knowledge/odin-brain/.last-collect

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Action Queue card store and audit log (private draft bodies
# and recipient addresses).
outputs/operations/action-queue/queue.json
outputs/operations/action-queue/disposition-log.jsonl

# OPERATIONAL DATA: quarantined wreck files. `scripts/utils/quarantine.py` always
# writes into a `.quarantine/` directory beside the original, so one rule covers
# every state file it ever quarantines (2026-08-29).
**/.quarantine/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: dead-letter queue records (recipient and body payloads).
outputs/operations/dead-letter

# OPERATIONAL DATA: /implement run artifacts (per-run tmp and trajectory logs).
outputs/operations/implement/_tmp/*
!outputs/operations/implement/_tmp/.gitkeep
outputs/operations/implement/_trajectory_*.jsonl

# OPERATIONAL DATA: per-skill personal customization overrides; the shared
# layer ({skill}.toml) is committed, the personal layer stays local.
config/skill-custom/*.user.toml

# OPERATIONAL DATA: memlog working-memory files backing long-running skills.
**/.memlog.md

# OPERATIONAL DATA: eval-capture staged drafts written inside the engine before
# 2026-10-16; eval-flag.py now stages them under the registry name
# skill-eval-drafts, and this keeps any older copy out of git.
**/evals/outcomes/_staged/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: data directories never belong in the engine; data lives in
# the data repository, resolved by registry name.
/threads/
/crm/
/outputs/
/knowledge/
/context/
/plans/
/datastore/
/_archive/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: legacy two-layer trees from the retired executive model. Old
# clones may still hold them; nothing in the engine reads them.
/corporate/
/personal/

# SECRET: proprietary licensed fonts, not redistributable in a public repo.
# Adopters supply their own; the marp theme degrades to a system fallback.
.claude/skills/marp/themes/fonts/GT-Standard-*.woff2
.claude/skills/marp/themes/fonts/31CHorizontalT03-*.woff2

# REBUILDABLE: plugin and marketplace build output (scripts/dev/build-plugins.py).
/dist/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: Canopus freeze state from the lifecycle retired 2026-08-07.
# Nothing writes it, but old clones still hold it; deleting this line once
# staged a 115 KB history file into this public repository. Remove it only after
# the leftovers are gone from every clone.
.canopus/

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the per-worktree bootstrap receipt and the two pytest logs
# yard-bootstrap.sh writes (scripts/herdr/heading-os-yard/). Worthless in any
# other checkout. Literal names on purpose: `.claude/` is mostly tracked source.
.claude/.yard-bootstrap-status
.claude/.yard-bootstrap-tree-clean.log
.claude/.yard-bootstrap-canary.log

# OPERATIONAL DATA: scratch slash-commands minted by the skill-creator plugin's
# eval harness inside the tracked `.claude/commands/`. Its run_eval.py unlinks
# and sweeps them; this is the belt for a SIGKILL.
.claude/commands/*-skill-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].md

# REBUILDABLE: Hugging Face model and tokenizer downloads.
.cache/huggingface

# OPERATIONAL DATA: the content-guard probe file the gate tests wrote inside this
# repository. Ignored so a probe left by a killed run can never be committed.
tests/_precommit_guard_probe-*

# REBUILDABLE: what Claude Code writes into a mod's folder on each load (API
# type declarations and a tsconfig.json extending them; 2026-10-10).
scripts/claude-mods/*/.claude-plugin/types/
scripts/claude-mods/*/tsconfig.json
